ype {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438376} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f29ea4e-5810-5f1f-8d38-3af5b722ca38" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4bd52ca-a205-555d-b11b-af034890ac41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438378} {:answer/id #uuid "80894a1d-f190-53cc-8c63-380f026a2360" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4bd52ca-a205-555d-b11b-af034890ac41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438378} :answer-field/id #uuid "750e5491-90bd-5c37-88f3-add2d8d905de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439218} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf619b4-1886-5820-adc3-81526c6d2929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438380} {:answer/id #uuid "6bda3536-0b94-5e44-9742-a2487520d230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bda3536-0b94-5e44-9742-a2487520d230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438381} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d195a39-4057-5477-9c72-c735cd1d4ad7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439219}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b9771ce-36d1-5cb6-a7ee-84e40d892ce6" :question/math-academy-id "q-66508" :question/problem "![](images/23/239490fd3be930412d4f67ff89244607a5019d91f201bc4e579410b5610a18ed.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/c7/c728d173c13a1e7b3bcad0e9f0284c97f2ca075c795dcb1f38ed086c19cc0504.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graphs I and IV, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graphs I  and IV show one-to-one functions. This means that  these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graphs II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7166ecf3-b50b-508e-9ed3-8ed61ef5ae61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438382} {:answer/id #uuid "f55eb19c-2f9e-55bf-96bf-393b353a9fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7166ecf3-b50b-508e-9ed3-8ed61ef5ae61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438382} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c282a3-ae0f-5137-bd44-fd265e629295" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4146f84-975f-51a7-8ac3-491200ec7ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438384} {:answer/id #uuid "95464e11-21eb-503c-969d-6b1b3d80b5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4146f84-975f-51a7-8ac3-491200ec7ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438384} :answer-field/id #uuid "14c61d66-c6e4-51dc-a0f5-b4828f76eb01" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c82069ca-19bf-56ee-9cd9-d805058547a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438386} {:answer/id #uuid "2b3cb73d-abf1-5101-9683-fdd7d581e2ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c82069ca-19bf-56ee-9cd9-d805058547a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438386} :answer-field/id #uuid "69550b73-4350-5542-be35-a03df4f9e490" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439222} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5fb294-358d-514e-bebe-8b88e070a1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438388} {:answer/id #uuid "13ff8217-4eae-5f89-83fc-66f923d9914a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13ff8217-4eae-5f89-83fc-66f923d9914a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438389} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ae256c7-3428-50d2-aa08-96e73977c7af" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d080acd-916c-5650-8a33-fa75e4ad9891" :question/math-academy-id "q-66509" :question/problem "![](images/be/be5b7625ad6f540f6769b121f52ccad69b669dbf764fc3bb68f89c99f066f145.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/bf/bfc7d94de67ceeb0c4aaa0988c117fce7f15242c2f3d223eecd8f0eb77135d7e.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graph IV, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph IV shows a one-to-one function. This means that  the function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459ca46e-eefb-5abd-9d1f-bfc45ab98061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438398} {:answer/id #uuid "035c1b02-9d7f-5f89-80c1-6ac8547e9e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459ca46e-eefb-5abd-9d1f-bfc45ab98061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438398} :answer-field/id #uuid "812fbc6b-d477-5628-93ef-37f1a61cdbaa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2e21695-9155-5372-8ce0-0af55699648f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438400} {:answer/id #uuid "58f5e743-7bd3-51ff-b5a7-1709ffb9ae0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2e21695-9155-5372-8ce0-0af55699648f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438400} :answer-field/id #uuid "697f4273-ecc9-5ca7-bf4e-cdb2d52fb55f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51930d2-65ad-57ec-9bdd-d1a7bef0954b" :answer