ese are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72895eac-ca3e-581f-9aad-01c047ba0ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513127} {:answer/id #uuid "e7827826-ec07-5997-b0b3-84bf7b1677d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72895eac-ca3e-581f-9aad-01c047ba0ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513127} :answer-field/id #uuid "1126b642-1027-5e3b-bd61-baa2f89bad30" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81df2964-3139-5ca7-b39f-1ea35cde5ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513135} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a251ae-b498-5622-865b-cfe3e8129b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7a251ae-b498-5622-865b-cfe3e8129b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513178} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d2c5548-3df4-5db5-9aeb-2db410adb01e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b09c7c62-8c22-556d-9fd1-f3b3db08c32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513148} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0704c-c1f6-5ea3-84f5-177140a1f2df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b09c7c62-8c22-556d-9fd1-f3b3db08c32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513148} :answer-field/id #uuid "41775d15-4b6f-5681-8fdb-1d1cc3eab76c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424c841a-fe27-52bb-9971-8c3c6a1f56cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513111} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8c0a05-20fc-559d-8491-77873d20901b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c8c0a05-20fc-559d-8491-77873d20901b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513133} :answer-field/id #uuid "b696151c-39ef-5f32-b33f-36cfdb48a420" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513151}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fca0faec-4871-5aa2-a939-0f9e32c7c7a5" :question/problem "![](images/86/86789a860ad2ca40419dbf47bb2939865e42c3316f162d07abace5f2efe9a05d.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain; an open circle excludes its endpoint.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nGraph positions: **I.** upper left; **II.** upper right; **III.** lower left; **IV.** lower right." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/45/450a431d00c33e12a60cf22d1e108c6147c6fa1ed0276068879e7d6008ea843e.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graphs II, IV, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, these graphs show one-to-one functions. As a result, these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58e72d70-cbf5-508d-8366-8222c736acd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513117} {:answer/id #uuid "d50b87f4-3005-5004-9a34-f8d97a15d60a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58e72d70-cbf5-508d-8366-8222c736acd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513117} :answer-field/id #uuid "09df5e92-d025-53f0-9070-39d15dfa8acb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65c3921f-0976-578f-bc93-a3e6822265f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513121} {:answer/id #uuid "9967ac84-e916-5b19-b89c-af095f066689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65c3921f-0976-578f-bc93-a3e6822265f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513121} :answer-field/id #uuid "476c3ada-63df-5ed0-9dbf-90b2ad2d02c7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030c1d4b-5a1a-5b9e-9cb7-cbee69cd0a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513090} {:answer/id #uuid "7682d7a7-de8b-5723-869b-3ead5d1258c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "030c1d4b-5a1a-5b9e-9cb7-cbee69cd0a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513090} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae353d0d-0d81-5063-a16d-07440e3264ca" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0d812fc-a440-516b-85ea-2f33ef68dbd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513158} {:answer/id #uuid "c5030c69-71f8-5fe4-bbeb-949065bd3921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5030c69-71f8-5fe4-bbeb-949065bd3921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513161} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66af6e9-d19d-5498-81e4-8cd816437ffb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513165}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fcef0170-a665-534f-b2df-558936bcb2e4" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8eda72cfe3c20e37b59138513b963781740e9b7d892b8cfa71caa7e0502ff83a.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nEach graph shows its entire domain; an open circle excludes its endpoint.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nGraph positions: **I.** upper left; **II.** upper right; **III.** lower left; **IV.** lower right." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/1a/1a29e16b93980feb428e3386ee6fc95bc6afdce3d698f01a280303f6ff272597.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graphs I, II, IV, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, these graphs show one-to-one functions. As a result, these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graph III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124284 :question/id #uuid "b6722faa-6069-59c1-8861-75b8207b0a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-3962" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d965e0b1087ad45206dd9259c963609f556bf5803af47ab18006bf40dffb2557.png)\n\n     \n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $(-3,-1]$\n\n- $(0,4]$\n\n- $[-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.   \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-1].$  Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/24/245484a6a77160a5f5892738a7e1f8e488f6df8e4ba990bbc94ae964c3305525.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $(0,4]$ and $[-2,2)$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/47/4737a1460e1abd4edc200404407fef10761f038d9a29e52ba0f8c3e8c69bb93f.png)\n\n          \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4b078b7-f5a3-5e10-8da4-739f031e9cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438214} {:answer/id #uuid "8c292220-45e3-5b72-bba6-cb8a5c0646b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c292220-45e3-5b72-bba6-cb8a5c0646b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438215} :answer-field/id #uuid "251d1017-18ef-5bc9-9883-11eca3e38d83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48ad9111-5ff9-5808-834a-73627abed3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438216} {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438217} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d06f78-7466-5d54-950d-cb989daacc0e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438218} {:answer/id #uuid "00a2f1ae-0f2a-55b3-bef4-eabad652d111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438218} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c704ed7-9a63-5c1b-90d0-bdb2e302d80f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439138}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8099f21-9137-5121-a075-a61a4c5ae84b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36039" :question/problem "![](images/93/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-4,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,1)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/cb/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78aca4cb-e874-5654-89d1-3d26d0e9075a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438248} {:answer/id #uuid "56ebc0ee-62bb-5743-905c-8d3b1f4543aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56ebc0ee-62bb-5743-905c-8d3b1f4543aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4850d87-ba31-5f2e-a2c9-896106eec279" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dae7370-d996-56fe-936b-343de836684b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438250} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fe8981-13df-58ff-ab19-42ab217c7691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dae7370-d996-56fe-936b-343de836684b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 