l that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-2,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,0)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,0]$ and $x\\in (0,2).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/46/46e1daf2cb9025b6a736f223fbe168ea32b66302cebea23ca3a2d473e78b77b3.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $(-3,0)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ed3670f7c67d60c7739ee35d66943b8341b2a49faa97546242609dd39afabc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aba0040-ed79-59d5-8f0c-1da6506dcb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242260} {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242517} {:answer/id #uuid "a34d8087-ba76-52a1-b9de-dc8c243066f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242609} {:answer/id #uuid "bc11acb5-2479-5b6f-8d5c-5023dd267a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242829} {:answer/id #uuid "d159698e-637b-5ec8-b7bd-777c6c74a47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242517} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24403e2-8bbf-51d7-83c0-df91fa667cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243783}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8649e7a-85fc-57ea-9a08-e015b963b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-108791" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4fec1c187ae2eaaf40461775425b31d896bdc63bc99233277d6f6bac8949315d.png)\n\nDetermine the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,5].$ \n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in (1,3).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/eb/eb544795c61be7dd87568e6def10fc907c3554b603c3b344f88ac2a8ff847f8d.png)\n\n- Among the given options, the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ is invertible is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$ On this domain, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/40/4059a1ad684023640358af6ee38f0967957336578eb93b3299c9c842e7ce108f.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ca8803d-d3a1-5a90-b629-eaffa681a751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241421} {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242216} {:answer/id #uuid "75a09077-b272-55f9-9ec5-02e4cb5e59f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242225} {:answer/id #uuid "874dd0bf-adab-5f92-915f-11ce125271a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242365} {:answer/id #uuid "b8117842-6e5d-53d4-bbd5-db19b3700bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242216} :answer-field/id #uuid "7223ab10-697e-58e6-b5d8-13b63f336aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243661}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8e69af0-0327-53e8-9129-272172fb2aff" :question/math-academy-id "q-108795" :question/problem "![](images/de/def2afaad6d1f74ca3ac8833ed6e35efea1296b324ef5a14c2d9513983a63456.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-2,4].$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [-2,0].$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-2$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/03/033b9e827caf4fc89d4b179c769f5115254c811953f93caf33d0959bfd063235.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [0,4].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/4c/4c91aa95131758065b1d8befe7c69895dc51d2f984a04cc8f06932a32e552792.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [0,4]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f108dd6c-61c1-5717-8270-831f0354507f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438184} {:answer/id #uuid "c64a7a6a-c767-501b-8788-7c590bc536b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c64a7a6a-c767-501b-8788-7c590bc536b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438185} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b129ee-af9a-5e28-9358-1428d9acd89e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1299406e-f829-5fd4-8425-b85b65f7d4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438186} {:answer/id #uuid "eb523abd-ddb9-5635-ac9c-2ff66317cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1299406e-f829-5fd4-8425-b85b65f7d4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438186} :answer-field/id #uuid "926e0c3c-cd97-51cc-9746-082bf755755f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af648e1c-82fc-509a-86a4-bb4d1e1ddc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438188} {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438189} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77279af-afdb-5c4b-87f9-0e122b9f690b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439123}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69ab5c8f-74d2-578a-ab14-a3f834908b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-36002" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c51c5a4de562e5a3301ea76afc6af57b459acd4c46e5c65d54afc226d883a137.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,1)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [0,3)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,0]$ and $x\\in [0,3).$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/00/00a80dde24ca012e0282362224c8b63764f5e149a8bfcda9c76ff4eb958fa93a.png)\n\n \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/9e/9ea54918e2ef4310b58e9cf8a0c9b1f9757a404d97dbbfd9e5b037af2193f38c.png)\n\n \n\nHence, the correct answer is 'I and III only''."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e496da34-dbaf-5186-8e70-09599d4e42f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438190} {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438191} :answer-field/id #uuid "482ac440-f320-503b-99d7-eb74230b2bc9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438192} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcd2979-e497-5817-b474-8325f90706bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438192} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d241933-0dfc-5f49-ba97-b39545dc4a25" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c808cf-3477-5af3-b1f2-145c26c92a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438194} {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4056b817-e800-5678-8e9e-22469e604236" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439126}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "544516cf-cdec-5de8-af07-1ff7e5be101e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36004" :question/problem "![](images/15/1597ad53471d0d9b44812c5caa31bcb160cfa150d1df9a9314447fa49e62ccff.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-6,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-6,4)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [4,10)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-6,0]$ and $x\\in [4,10).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/7c/7cb282e3fa66af801ff03816973d5f5f1d0cb41e39d08a8addd27d7aa9c5b9df.png)\n\n      \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[-6,4]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/00/000953609a7b3e13ad09473ead62f96aa895c7f94aa618884e69883595004fd4.png)\n\n \n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6dd990f-2330-5d0c-81b4-6370f4d92329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438196} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa5f1a4-0dd6-545a-95f5-013d457374c6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438198} {:answer/id #uuid "37107bf0-d7a1-5dde-a57d-5db8ff5c2424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438198} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7ed940-ad9d-549b-8ff8-c6ed363707ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65a72c59-feca-5579-98db-917865bf0995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438200} {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438201} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7aa9bfc-97c1-53ea-b5a1-715f3992c90c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439129}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f06fc453-0309-58aa-ad2f-fecdd1ab38c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36008" :question/problem "![](images/27/279c3cd6084423d913186f4ba467ea50d0f794cf54773785777cb8841f5c2ca1.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [-1,3]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-1]$ and on $x\\in [0,1].$  Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/03/0388335095ed530ce07d278f82be5eb3bff14859db64b6e9ec47da27861bb657.png)\n\n    \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval. $x\\in [-1,3]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/52/522b5661aaf9b7640c305b8cefd06f49cc8eed590f3ae736fc6720e6165bc3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323742 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88cfd433-113f-5181-b46c-34920cbe5bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438208} {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0273b980-43eb-564c-872d-0589397d574e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890e79b7-dfdd-538c-8e9a-7abc3f553b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438210} {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211} :answer-field/id #uuid "5568fe44-2db6-5364-963c-2b0dbd971f58" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} {:answer/id #uuid "cfff16d0-eaff-5775-853f-d6b2f96cf631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f018c0-f200-5146-8568-3810e8f2e7b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d31db013-e3f7-5fe2-aefa-8428da418673" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-2,3]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/53/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/63/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbc8c33-86dd-598e-8ee7-fa04f2bc7ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321504} {:answer/id #uuid "3b34c587-aba0-515e-a326-983fc0c9bb25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321602} {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322259} {:answer/id #uuid "c42fd510-9a4e-5f4a-8ea1-cce741552a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322670} {:answer/id #uuid "fed6c880-f715-5a34-9e47-e4d3b005ddd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322259} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfb24cc-9668-58dd-abc6-31788a668fce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6425603b-0808-58ba-b2d2-92cbdbcccb68" :question/math-academy-id "q-36061" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d4353286b5d1668d2a67539db8b1fd27227872b1f5a2eaa5fd6015716f255b0.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,4).$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [1,4).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/a7/a709558673202ef4a7835dcea6e23b7ec5b13684272c56023058223c01fb8061.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [-3,1].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/5a/5a65e71f571e9510580ba5fe105a6eac48acfe4564c5a6bf76371c2bf09ff651.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [-3,1]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc69b98-00eb-5840-b90d-c96ba4931e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438228} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a6aac-97fe-50a0-8beb-d1323671d7f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a97abe-d55d-5007-b4fd-6937cc34e17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438230} {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231} :answer-field/id #uuid "6639d61d-bf93-5072-838b-4370ba49c0ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf0f901-76be-5f84-b0ee-c5cd9c1a5306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0537b4-3665-5585-a12b-bb1d508ad121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6815ae09-6f05-5b7b-9ca9-f709c3e26769" :question/math-academy-id "q-36066" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2065775ae6372e8c820b5e2f19f6f105e032dcd37db1e32e04af5bfa6a4faf9.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$ and $x\\in (0,2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/3c/3c5bc724ee29aee7bef2790012bf0e73ce1ed087134213dbad36a670fd136a36.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[1,4)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/03/03b9d70513a4ef99b39c9f05d0c0ac803f8e5611d0967015e9c1d9c0f45bd418.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438242} {:answer/id #uuid "c6255188-de6f-5359-b3ce-b11fa26ffa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438242} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f5bf02-6bde-5643-acf0-85bec1bb3263" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c10d5b55-5751-534e-848f-312026170d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438244} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438245} :answer-field/id #uuid "edb61cc5-3d51-546d-9186-fa06d6294e86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438246} {:answer/id #uuid "d1341450-0c68-5e67-bd60-bd2b0eef6a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438246} :answer-field/id #uuid "781dd2b1-5946-5698-92e6-edc4b9e58172" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439152}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24e31b-6e93-5c8b-93d0-5c6b5852eeb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36934" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d8/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/bc/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137d4f4e-74af-5d41-b80a-53934c9dd028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513035} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4ea36e-8e0c-52de-bf81-a2a939c9d472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd4ea36e-8e0c-52de-bf81-a2a939c9d472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513079} :answer-field/id #uuid "523762b1-5a6f-5bc9-9c5f-40cf749f2fa6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c32bb1-32b3-5f2a-9a16-528b55e0e374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513030} {:answer/id #uuid "652bf4b1-f67c-53f8-803c-b0ecdf18e329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "652bf4b1-f67c-53f8-803c-b0ecdf18e329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513058} :answer-field/id #uuid "d00c1508-a5bb-5bd1-aac8-883af6e66c84" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a58b7aef-9928-5d29-9b06-bfd7f833b4da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513067} {:answer/id #uuid "cbcbfa36-7793-50b7-add2-58f15ee36dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbcbfa36-7793-50b7-add2-58f15ee36dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513077} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6b3a4e-16cb-5aa7-a937-e322b7dac4b1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513088}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a972469-92c6-5025-b8f5-75835bec6279" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efc2a0fcf4999a4ab32cdd5957a87ec7bf782cdb1ecac743551fd0509b983f6b.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nI. $x\\in (-2,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in [0,4]$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-1,4]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- On interval I, $x\\in (-2,0]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval II, $x\\in [0,4]$, the function is invertible. Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the restricted graph at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- On interval III, $x\\in [-1,4]$, the function is **not** invertible. Some horizontal lines will intersect the restricted graph more than once.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46145733-2a91-595a-9887-3c27f126163b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513051} {:answer/id #uuid "4e283f29-9e66-57a6-8d2d-ce7602205610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e283f29-9e66-57a6-8d2d-ce7602205610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513054} :answer-field/id #uuid "b279fd60-6bf8-5bfe-a026-b8526fbfbc01" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1587b9b5-0f0f-5f7c-80b4-aa4404d6fad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513036} {:answer/id #uuid "b14ad64f-3349-56a7-9acc-9b3cb7b991f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14ad64f-3349-56a7-9acc-9b3cb7b991f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513069} :answer-field/id #uuid "b86fde67-1d4b-5eef-b9b2-b000c129805f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f2333a7-48da-5f82-9698-853051ad6c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513040} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b44efe-11d8-5921-be10-61234006e63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1b44efe-11d8-5921-be10-61234006e63e" :